    <h2>The Four Blizzard Groups Explained</h2>
    <p>DQ's Blizzard lineup divides naturally into four categories. Understanding which group a flavor belongs to helps you choose confidently:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Classic Candy-Bar Blizzards</strong> — Oreo, M&amp;M's, Butterfinger, Snickers, Heath. These rely on familiar candy flavors blended into soft serve. Oreo leads the pack.</li>
      <li><strong>Baked-Good Blizzards</strong> — Cookie Dough, Brownie Batter, Choco Brownie Extreme. Richer, denser, more calorie-dense. Best for chocolate and baked-flavor fans.</li>
      <li><strong>Royal Blizzards</strong> — Standard flavors with a warm filled center (fudge, peanut butter, strawberry). Cost about $1 more per size. The Royal Oreo is the most popular upgrade on the entire menu.</li>
      <li><strong>Seasonal Specials</strong> — Rotate throughout the year. Pumpkin Pie in fall, Peppermint Hot Cocoa in winter, summer specials like Dipped Strawberry Cheesecake and S'mores.</li>
    </ul>

